+
+\[ \parbox{0.86\linewidth}{\raggedright W\textsubscript{ℓ}(r, O, q, z) = C\textsubscript{ℓ}(r, O, q, z) if z\textsubscript{ℓ} ≠ –, otherwise (1 − ψ\textsubscript{ℓ})·C\textsubscript{ℓ}(r, O, q, z[ℓ↦N]) + ψ\textsubscript{ℓ}·C\textsubscript{ℓ}(r, O, q, z[ℓ↦L]);} \tag{C.5} \]
+
+\[ \text{C\textsubscript{ℓ}(r, O, q, z) = max\{ v\textsubscript{ℓ} − D·λ\textsubscript{ℓ} − R\textsubscript{ℓ}, E(r, O, q, z, \{ℓ\}) \};} \tag{C.6} \]
+
+\[ \parbox{0.86\linewidth}{\raggedright E(r, O, q, z, B) = 0 if r = 2, otherwise Σ over G ⊆ O∖B of β\textsuperscript{g}·(1 − β)\textsuperscript{m − g}·V(r + 1, O∖G, q, z),} \tag{C.7} \]
+
+where g = \textbar G\textbar, m = \textbar O∖B\textbar, and β is the outside-demand rate of Equation (B.2): ½ in the main and development sets and
+0.3 in the holdout.
+
+Before a landlord has answered, the tenant cannot know its listing's lowest rent, because a sound listing's cost
+lies anywhere from \$20 to \$80 under the ask. The tenant therefore plans with the average (\$50 under the ask, plus the
+\$25 margin) and replans with the true rent once an answer arrives. On the main evaluation set the \texttt{pricing} tenant
+earns \$307.32 a world and the \texttt{stated} tenant \$266.89, which is below the reachable reference, so \texttt{stated} is not a
+best policy for the v14 task prompt.
